<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lycīum</span></b>  (less correctly <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lycēum</span></b> , v.
		Ellendt ad <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 1, 21, 98</span></i>), i,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λύκειον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a gymnasium very near
				Athens, in which Aristotle taught</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 1, 21, 98</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ac. 1, 4,
			17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Div. 1, 13, 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 31,
				24, 18</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 20, 5,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>The upper gymnasium of Cicero's Tusculan villa, with
				a library in it</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 5, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 3,
			8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A gymnasium of the emperor Hadrian at his Tiburtine
				villa</i>, <i><span class="en">Spart. Hadr.
		27</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
